+## Append-only bce3f075-security-02: five security providers and shared verdict
+
+61 schema rows and three previously hidden `common.POLICY` business fields now
+have exact parser/reader/owning-schema/current-vs-target domains and full concrete
+future specifications. Current totals: 1,225 rows, 4,379 case bodies: 1,140 narrow
+source/definition passed, 3,239 future not-run. **No semantic acceptance**.
+This batch adds 65 narrow C0 definitions and 256 future full-boundary cases.
+
+Current productive configuration functions were called directly through their
+existing `testContract` exports, not replaced or modified. They are the exact
+functions called by actual `provider.execute`; C0 does not execute those providers'
+scanner/network/runtime capabilities, isolated worker, database/lease/grant or
+original F-EFFECT obligations. `common.result` probes use fabricated source
+findings and explicit proposed resolved policy to check existing verdict math;
+they cannot stand in for actual scanner-generated findings. Future fixtures use
+exact producer-generated finding ID requirements and real source/tool/database/
+image/deployment/manifest/lease evidence, not the C0 `case-finding` identity.
+
+### Current semantics and explicit validator deltas
+
+Current `strict-v1` is a **business preset**, not a protocol excuse for hardcoded
+blocking severities, active-threat blocking and missing-fix blocking. The current
+parser rejects authored alternatives; three new source rows enumerate the real
+pure verdict readers and source alternatives. A proposed complete single owned
+policy has all five scoped timeouts, full header rules, all three verdict fields
+and waiver list; no hidden `POLICY`/`PROFILES` or old selector fallback. Its strict
+schema and exact uniqueness/HSTS semantic checks are C0 proposals, not implemented
+production owner/loader validation. Actual stronger runtime deadlines/grants and
+source trust remain separate dependencies, not duplicated authors.
+
+Root provider unknown keys are ignored, policy-root unknown keys reject, waiver
+entry unknown keys are ignored, null waivers become empty, and Date.parse accepts
+a date-only expiry that the owning schema rejects. Actual rule parsing accepts
+33 added rules while owning schema caps that array at 32; current resolved rules
+still cap at 64. Unknown removal IDs are ignored; removal happens before
+replacement. A present-kind rule discards its value even when the schema rejects
+that supplied value. Target invalid/unused/retired author rejection remains a
+future same-boundary requirement; these current gaps are not target PASS.
+
+A 400-digit HSTS threshold string passes current owning schema and current rule
+parser and becomes nonfinite under `Number`. Proposed owner semantic checks
+require positive **safe integer seconds** and reject that control before effects;
+this source safety correction is proposed/unapproved. The current preserved HSTS
+threshold is 31,536,000 seconds, an owned business rule, not model/API capacity.
+Exact rule-value A/B cases use their actual equals predicate, not a fictional
+numeric threshold when the chosen rule is string-valued.
+
+Header findings always carry `status:affected`; with current active-threat flag
+true, changing high to low severity still blocks. Future cases explicitly observe
+visible severity change without claiming gate admission. Waivers keep original
+findings visible. Absolute `expiresAt` continues to be evaluated against actual
+`Date.now`, including recovery: immutable CONFIG does not freeze the expiry clock.
+Reason changes are disclosure only; expiry/matching actual producer ID affect
+acceptance. `scannerError:error` is internal copied diagnostic metadata, not read
+by the result decision; actual capability errors propagate. The proposed owner
+rejects this unused field even equal-valued, not inventing a new error-policy knob.
+
+### Explicit source-candidate continuation
+
+85 additional source-line-reviewed candidate records give 149 combined records;
+4,493 of the original 4,642 remain unreviewed. Of reviewed records, 27 still carry
+precise open guard/platform/runtime-owner obligations. Separate unmatched syntax
+omissions include header response cap 65,536, disclosure/hash truncation limits,
+full preset literal provenance and actual Trivy runtime database-policy defaults
+48 hours / 7 days / 8 GiB per file. Database evidence projects that runtime policy;
+it must not become a second provider-owned database author. Numeric schema/count/
+size guards are not automatically excluded merely because their container is task
+or finding data. Unsupported real scanner/database/platform inputs remain explicit.
+
+Batch scripts, source/input/test/commit/tree/dirty/untracked identities, original
+checkpoint inputs and raw successes/failures are retained. Reproduction:
